    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0xB8BE; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Cold intake-cam target surface. FUN 000bda64 interpolates it by RPM/50 byte ffff11ae and Q7 normalized-BFS scheduler snapshot ffff102c and writes ffff1c5e. FUN 000bdc66 uses it at raw coolant &lt;=106 and blends it with warm/main target 0000b43a between raw coolant 106 and 131 before the result enters the intake CVTC target path. Code proves the cold intake-cam target role, raw coolant selection, centered byte representation, and column coordinate at raw*100/128 percent of the fixed BFS reference. The target-vehicle capture stays above the warm threshold. The cold-start replay in JK08A.cvtc.md validates this surface through the coolant blend, while its stationary cold band follows idle source byte ffff1553 and leaves the direct cold lookup dynamically untested. The output conversion (x-128)*0.5 crank degrees follows the intake edge-phase unit shared with 0000b43a: the cold target enters the same ffff2326 path that FUN 0004d2a6 compares with actual bytes ffff2442/ffff2443. The Cylinder Filling physical name remains a source-derived candidate. Result disposition: consumer. Definition address projected from JK08A 0000b53a through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: cold intake-cam target in the stock intake CVTC descriptor block at 0x000C386C. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
