  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xC678" flags="0x0">
    <title>Intake CVTC Target Correction - High-Detonation State</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0xAEDE; 4 rows x 4 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Conditional intake-cam target correction. When ffff2466.bit6 is set, FUN 000bda64 calculates clamp_u8(output_0000b43a - output_0000ab5a + 128); when the bit is clear, it bypasses this map. The corrected target is written to ffff1c5c and enters the intake CVTC target path. Code proves the conditional intake-cam correction path and centered raw arithmetic. The target-vehicle capture contains zero samples with ffff2466.bit6 set, so this branch has no dynamic validation. The correction is subtracted from the 0000b43a output count for count, so it carries the intake edge-phase unit of 0.5 crank degrees per count. The high-detonation meaning of the selector and the Cylinder Filling axis name remain catalog candidates. Result disposition: consumer. Definition address projected from JK08A 0000ab5a through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: intake-cam correction table in the stock intake CVTC descriptor block at 0x000C386C. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via axis evidence: indexed_by].</description>
