  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xE9A5" flags="0x0">
    <title>Exhaust CVTC Target - Standstill Override</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0x8E74; 1 rows x 1 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Standstill exhaust-VTC override target. While ffff246c bit 1 is set (operational enable, engine speed between ROM8[0x8e3b] and ROM8[0x8e3a], coarse vehicle speed at or below ROM8[0x8e3c], P/N position switch ON in ffff244f bit 2) and latch ffff2478 bit 4 is clear, FUN 000bfe88 writes clamp_u8(ROM8[0x8e36]+128) to ffff137e at 000c01f4 in place of the coolant-selected map byte; the demand flag, both bank enables, and the duty controller then follow it. Once both banks have tracked the target within ROM8[0x8e16]=6 counts for 0.512 s the latch sets and the byte returns to 128 until the operational enable falls. The stroke is the actuation of the exhaust valve timing control learning, whose tail in the same function captures the integrator of error stage 000c1152 on a clean bank release. Raw 0 commands the neutral byte 128, which still replaces the map byte and can set the latch; the stroke is removed through ROM8[0x8e3b]=255. Stock value 40 is +20 degCA of exhaust retard. The byte is added to the 128 center in the same raw units as surface 0000b33a and target ffff2327, so it carries the code-proven 0.5 crank degrees per count of the actual bytes that monitor 0008f168 compares with the target. It is single-copy and not a Map Switching family, so a change applies to every map slot. The 2026-09-17 captures of a Map 3 image with neutral surfaces show the override as eight excursions to raw 168 starting as the engine passed 1800 RPM at rest. Definition address projected from JK08A 00008e36 through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: unique 8-byte constant block 28 14 00 00 50 24 02 02 at 0x008E74 referenced as literal 0x00008E74 by the target exhaust CVTC conditioner 000c5b64 that follows the target exhaust accessor 000c5a44; byte 0 is read at 000c5e46 through the pool slot 000c5fd4 as the source conditioner 000bfe88 reads byte 0 at 000c01a4 through 000c0290.</description>
