    <title>Exhaust CVTC Standstill Override - RPM Floor</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0x8E79; 1 rows x 1 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Engine-speed floor of the standstill exhaust-VTC override. FUN 000bfe88 sets ffff24ab bit 0 at 000bfee4 when engine-speed byte ffff11ae reaches this value and clears it when the byte plus hysteresis ROM8[0x86e1]=4 falls below it. Stock value 36 is 1800 RPM with release below 1600 RPM. The flag is one input of override predicate ffff246c bit 1 and has no other consumer, so raw 255 keeps the predicate clear at every reachable engine speed and removes the override stroke, its latch ffff2478 bit 4, and the opportunity it gives the exhaust valve timing control learning. Definition address projected from JK08A 00008e3b through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: byte 5 of the unique 8-byte constant block at 0x008E74; read by the target exhaust CVTC conditioner 000c5b64 at 000c5baa through the pool slot 000c5d94 as the source conditioner 000bfe88 reads byte 5 at 000bfece through 000c0034. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
