  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x76CF" flags="0x0">
    <title>Injection Pulse Channel Multiplier</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0x14D45; 1 rows x 6 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Six-channel injection-pulse multiplier indexed directly by channel number 0..5. For a positive calculated pulse, FUN_0004eba2 multiplies by the selected byte, shifts the product right by 7, saturates to uint16, and writes the raw and transformed six-channel output arrays. All six stock cells are 128, so every channel uses multiplier 1.0. A set bit in override mask ffff22e0 bypasses this multiplier and selects word ffff2436. The trace proves channel indexing but does not establish the physical cylinder order; presentation labels remain generic channel numbers. Definition address projected from JK08A 000129c0 through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: target literals and reviewed homologous consumer topology. Static diagnostic context: INJ PULSE-B1 [code, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: writes].</description>
