  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xD6ED" flags="0x0">
    <title>MAF Factor</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0x8A4C; 1 rows x 1 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Unsigned airflow-unit scalar in the primary Base Fuel Schedule calculation. With Q=uint32[ffff1e38], F=ROM8[0x8a27], K=ROM16[0x9284], E=ROM8[0x88fb], and engine-speed count N, FUN 0003b75c forms min(floor(floor(F*K*Q/256)/(E*N)),0x726f9) before the final fixed-point conversion to ffff1e40. Stock F is 109. The A2L MAF Factor entry matches the byte's operational position, representation, and cross-ROM literal-pool signature and distinguishes it from K-Value. Homologous values are 133 for 1ND0A/1ND3B, 131 for JK78C, 109 for JK03A/JK08A, and 132 for JK00D. The engineering unit and multiplier remain source-derived pending hardware validation. J1979 Mode 01 PID 0x10 declares ROM8[0x83ec]/25600 g/s per count of the total quantity that the Base Fuel Schedule producer reproduces from A+B, which is 0.01477 kg/hr per count with stock 105, while F*0.0001 gives 0.0109 kg/hr per count; the A2L unit of F does not match the ECU's declared airflow. Definition address projected from JK08A 00008a27 through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: target literals and reviewed homologous consumer topology.</description>
