  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x5870" flags="0x0">
    <title>Engine Torque Base Term vs RPM</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0x179A2; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence candidate. RPM-indexed unsigned base term in the engine-torque calculation. FUN 00065c26 writes lookup M to ffff18c4 and calculates ffff2408=sat_u16(M-D+C), where D is proportional to current Base Fuel Schedule divided by ROM16[00009534] and C is a calibrated nonnegative correction. FUN 000659ae adds ffff2408 without rescaling to the signed centered output of Engine Torque Map 00010b8e. This continuous path establishes a common internal torque domain. In stock JK08A ROM8[000087f3]=32 makes C zero. The physical x*0.1 Nm conversion follows the Engine Torque Map catalog and requires hardware validation. Result disposition: consumer. Definition address projected from JK08A 000154a0 through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: reviewed JK08A-to-JK00D operands composed with unique JK00D-to-JK00C interpolation operands.</description>
