    <title>Map 3 - DFCO Hold RPM Threshold</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0xE0690; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Coolant-indexed held-request RPM threshold in DFCO request evaluator FUN 0004fbe2. Exact stock branch logic selects it after upstream DFCO mode bit 5 is already present in both current snapshot ffff2458 and previous snapshot ffff245a, subject to additional runtime gates. Common-definition Map 3 storage is projected from 0x14A51. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. The comparison is strict RPM/25 &gt; threshold. The Nissan A2L registry labels this address as the Bosch-family table, but exact JK08A code interpolates and selects it dynamically in stock operation. It is not an inactive-family calibration. Target-vehicle A/B evidence in patches/hardware-results.toml shows that stock request thresholds can coexist with complete suppression of the full 0x3f inhibit mask when the restore pair is changed. This table is a request gate, not an independently sufficient cut command. Result disposition: inline_comparison. Definition address projected from JK08A 000126e4 through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: target literals and reviewed homologous consumer topology. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
