  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x9E15" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 5 - Timing-State Addend - Warm DFCO Transition</title>
    <description>Exact JK00C. Address 0xE07B8; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Warm DFCO-transition eight-point timing-state addend. FUN 0004afdc selects it only when ffff244f.bit2 is clear, warm latch ffff41de.bit5 is set, upstream DFCO mode ffff2458.bit5 is set, and transition timer ffff2590 is nonzero. Common-definition Map 5 storage is projected from 0x1448B. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. The warm latch sets at raw coolant 110 and remains set down to raw 106, corresponding to 60 and 56 deg C under the exact diagnostic conversion. While ffff2458.bit5 is clear, ffff2590 reloads to 85; once the bit is set, the periodic scheduler decrements it. Selection therefore lasts for at most 85 scheduler counts, or 870.4 ms at the target-measured 10.24 ms period. A2L homology identifies the historical Idle Ignition Timing name. The alternate compositor branch of 0004bdc2 forms ffff1830=clamp_s8(ffff1a7d+ffff23ee-ffff23c5-64) at 0004be82 and shares the ffff2404 -&gt; ffff2378 -&gt; ffff12d6 -&gt; ffff11da -&gt; ffff11d4 chain of coefficient 1 with the low-seven surfaces, and J1979 PID 0x0E publishes ffff11d4 as A/2-64 degBTDC, so one count of this map is one crank degree of the declared coordinate. Index: implicit eight-point axis over ffff11b2 with saturation at element 7. Result disposition: writes (RAM ffff1511, site 0004b0d0). Definition address projected from JK08A 0001219e through JK08A-JK00C.definition-addresses.csv: target literals and reviewed homologous consumer topology. Static diagnostic context: IGN TIMING [candidate, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: writes].</description>
